{#
	ACF layout: rich_text — the body of a plain content page, such as the
	accessibility statement. Figma `doc-body` (22:175).

	Reuses `.article-body`, so prose written here is styled identically to a
	blog post body. One set of prose rules, not two.

	The measure is a column inside the 1200 container rather than
	`.container-narrow`, which centres. Every frame that draws this body — the
	2026-09 `doc-body` and the first revision's `article-body` before it — puts
	the 760 at x=560..1320, flush with the *start* edge of the 1200 container
	and not in the middle of it. Centring was never what the design asked for;
	it only looked close because a document page has nothing beside the column
	to measure it against.
#}

{% if section.content %}
	<section class="rich-text">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="article-body rich-text__body">{{ section.content|raw }}</div>
		</div>
	</section>
{% endif %}
